<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tarcondimotus I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 31 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as Tarcondimotus I Philantonios</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tarcondimotus I (died 31 BCE) was the ruler of a client kingdom in the Amanus mountains of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a>, recognised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> in 64 BCE. Ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hierapolis-castabala">Hierapolis-Castabala</a>, he supported the Roman commanders of the East in turn, took the surname Philantonios ('friend of Antony') and was killed fighting for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> in 31 BCE. His son Tarcondimotus II was later restored by Augustus.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tarcondimotus-i.jpg" alt="Tarcondimotus I" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bronze_coin_of_Tarkondimotos_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
